GTE entry wrappers: wire the full per-call register sequences (recover_regargs.py)

GTERT/GTERPS/GTERPT/GTERPT4_ @0x4139be/e7/0x413a29/0x413ac5 drive the three GTE
fragments FUN_00414016 (rotate: esi=vertex-in, edi=scratch @0x4604b6),
FUN_00414099 (translate/persp: esi=scratch, edi=vertex-in) and FUN_00413f85
(project/store: esi=scratch, edi=vertex-in, ebx=vertex-in, ebp=vertex-OUT)
purely through registers that Ghidra dropped. With the static _g_* defaults every
transform read/wrote the same fixed slots -> zero/garbage GTE output (Z=0 ->
idiv crash in DrawParticles' FUN_00436f00, wrong geometry everywhere).
Sequences recovered mechanically from dd2h.exe by tools/recover_regargs.py:
V0..V3 = 0x74c500/0x74c510/0x74c4e0/0x74c4f0, OUT0..OUT3 = 0x74c540/0x74c550/
0x74c520/0x74c530 (RT: rotate+translate only; RPS: 1 vertex; RPT: 3; RPT4: 4).

